---
# Per-host overrides. Copy to inventory/host_vars/<hostname>.yml.
#
# Anything from group_vars/all.yml can be narrowed here, because these
# are ordinary Ansible variables at a higher precedence. Metrics in
# particular are a plain per-host boolean rather than a fleet-wide list
# of opted-in hosts, and that is a deliberate difference from
# stortree_samba_hosts: whether this host publishes counters changes
# nothing for any other host, whereas every host's peer-trust
# provisioning depends on what the others decided about Samba. So there
# is nothing to keep in agreement here, and no list to edit in two
# places.

# This host alone stays quiet, on an otherwise metrics-enabled fleet.
stortree_metrics_enabled: false

# Or: this host alone publishes on its VPN interface, while the rest of
# the fleet stays on loopback. Named interfaces are resolved to an
# address at render time -- and a name that resolves to nothing fails
# the apply rather than falling back to a wildcard bind.
# stortree_metrics_bind:
#   - 127.0.0.1
#   - wg0
